1 "// The returned connection is of type *Conn."] [85 1 "// NewListener creates a Listener which accepts connections from an inner"] [86 1 "// Listener and wraps each connection with [Server]."] [87 1 "// The configuration config must be non-nil and must include"] [88 1 "// at least one certificate or else set GetCertificate."] [96 1 "// Listen creates a TLS listener accepting connections on the"] [97 1 "// given network address using net.Listen."] [98 1 "// The configuration config must be non-nil and must include"] [99 1 "// at least one certificate or else set GetCertificate."] [101 2 "// If this condition changes, consider updating http.Server.ServeTLS too."] [121 1 "// DialWithDialer connects to the given network address using dialer.Dial and"] [122 1 "// then initiates a TLS handshake, returning the resulting TLS connection. Any"] [123 1 "// timeout or deadline given in the dialer apply to connection and TLS"] [124 1 "// handshake as a whole."] [125 1 "//"] [126 1 "// DialWithDialer interprets a nil configuration as equivalent to the zero"] [127 1 "// configuration; see the documentation of [Config] for the defaults."] [128 1 "//"] [129 1 "// DialWithDialer uses context.Background internally; to specify the context,"] [130 1 "// use [Dialer.DialContext] with NetDialer set to the desired dialer."] [162 2 "// If no ServerName is set, infer the ServerName"] [163 2 "// from the hostname we're connecting to."] [165 3 "// Make a copy to avoid polluting argument or default."] [179 1 "// Dial connects to the given network address using net.Dial"] [180 1 "// and then initiates a TLS handshake, returning the resulting"] [181 1 "// TLS connection."] [182 1 "// Dial interprets a nil configuration as equivalent to"] [183 1 "// the zero configuration; see the documentation of Config"] [184 1 "// for the defaults."] [189 1 "// Dialer dials TLS connections given a configuration and a Dialer for the"] [190 1 "// underlying connection."] [192 2 "// NetDialer is the optional dialer to use for the TLS connections'"] [193 2 "// underlying TCP connections."] [194 2 "// A nil NetDialer is equivalent to the net.Dialer zero value."] [197 2 "// Config is the TLS configuration to use for new connections."] [198 2 "// A nil configuration is equivalent to the zero"] [199 2 "// configuration; see the documentation of Config for the"] [200 2 "// defaults."] [204 1 "// Dial connects to the given network address and initiates a TLS"] [205 1 "// handshake, returning the resulting TLS connection."] [206 1 "//"] [207 1 "// The returned [Conn], if any, will always be of type *[Conn]."] [208 1 "//"] [209 1 "// Dial uses context.Background internally; to specify the context,"] [210 1 "// use [Dialer.DialContext]."] [222 1 "// DialContext connects to the given network address and initiates a TLS"] [223 1 "// handshake, returning the resulting TLS connection."] [224 1 "//"] [225 1 "// The provided Context must be non-nil. If the context expires before"] [226 1 "// the connection is complete, an error is returned. Once successfully"] [227 1 "// connected, any expiration of the context will not affect the"] [228 1 "// connection."] [229 1 "//"] [230 1 "// The returned [Conn], if any, will always be of type *[Conn]."] [234 3 "// Don't return c (a typed nil) in an interface."] [240 1 "// LoadX509KeyPair reads and parses a public/private key pair from a pair of"] [241 1 "// files. The files must contain PEM encoded data. The certificate file may"] [242 1 "// contain intermediate certificates following the leaf certificate to form a"] [243 1 "// certificate chain. On successful return, Certificate.Leaf will be populated."] [256 1 "// X509KeyPair parses a public/private key pair from a pair of"] [257 1 "// PEM encoded data. On successful return, Certificate.Leaf will be populated."] [305 2 "// We don't need to parse the public key for TLS, but we so do anyway"] [306 2 "// to check that it looks sane and matches the private key."] [358 1 "// Attempt to parse the given private key DER block. OpenSSL 0.9.8 generates"] [359 1 "// PKCS #1 private keys by default, while OpenSSL 1.0.0 generates PKCS #8 keys."] [360 1 "// OpenSSL ecparam generates SEC1 EC private keys for ECDSA. We try all three."] [363 18 "// Return the PKCS#8 error if all parsing attempts fail."]] :go/pos {:name [19 9] :package [19 1]} :go/semis [[172 38]] :go/trails [[49 17] [63 17]]} (go/file "tls.go" :doc "Package tls partially implements TLS 1.2, as specified in RFC 5246,\nand TLS 1.3, as specified in RFC 8446.\n\n# FIPS 140-3 mode\n\nWhen the program is in [FIPS 140-3 mode], this package behaves as if only\nSP 800-140C and SP 800-140D approved protocol versions, cipher suites,\nsignature algorithms, certificate public key types and sizes, and key\nexchange and derivation algorithms were implemented. Others are silently\nignored and not negotiated, or rejected. This set may depend on the\nalgorithms supported by the FIPS 140-3 Go Cryptographic Module selected with\nGOFIPS140, and may change across Go versions.\n\n[FIPS 140-3 mode]: https://go.dev/doc/security/fips140\n" :imports [

